---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const frameImpactResult = await frameImpact(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const maintainHypothesesResult = await maintainHypotheses(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, frameImpactResult.accepted);
const selectDiagnosticsResult = await selectDiagnostics(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, maintainHypothesesResult.accepted);
const planRecoveryResult = await planRecovery(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, selectDiagnosticsResult.accepted);
const verifyRestorationResult = await verifyRestoration(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planRecoveryResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { frameImpact: frameImpactResult, maintainHypotheses: maintainHypothesesResult, selectDiagnostics: selectDiagnosticsResult, planRecovery: planRecoveryResult, verifyRestoration: verifyRestorationResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...frameImpactResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...maintainHypothesesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...selectDiagnosticsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planRecoveryResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...verifyRestorationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...frameImpactResult.checks, ...maintainHypothesesResult.checks, ...selectDiagnosticsResult.checks, ...planRecoveryResult.checks, ...verifyRestorationResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A diagnostic query would overload the database: enforce resource budgets in the query service. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (enforce resource budgets in the query service.) through the existing stage result for IncidentImpact; preserve exact source/version and the prior IncidentImpact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A rollback succeeds but data remains inconsistent: keep the incident open with a separate repair plan. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (keep the incident open with a separate repair plan.) through the existing stage result for IncidentImpact; preserve exact source/version and the prior IncidentImpact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — An action times out after execution: reconcile its actual state before retrying. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (reconcile its actual state before retrying.) through the existing stage result for IncidentImpact; preserve exact source/version and the prior IncidentImpact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — The commander changes mid-incident: transfer authority explicitly and preserve approvals. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (transfer authority explicitly and preserve approvals.) through the existing stage result for IncidentImpact; preserve exact source/version and the prior IncidentImpact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A model proposes an unapproved shell command: reject it and request an authorized runbook extension. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (reject it and request an authorized runbook extension.) through the existing stage result for IncidentImpact; preserve exact source/version and the prior IncidentImpact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, frameImpact: frameImpactResult, maintainHypotheses: maintainHypothesesResult, selectDiagnostics: selectDiagnosticsResult, planRecovery: planRecoveryResult, verifyRestoration: verifyRestorationResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
